{"rulings":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-bbc523c8","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment is materially inaccurate as written. In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs`, `temp_condition_factor()` no longer hardcodes the cold and hot divisors; it uses `params.temp_condition_low_divisor_c` and `params.temp_condition_high_divisor_c`. Those fields already exist on `ShrimpRuntimeParams` in `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`, have defaults of `10.0` and `8.0`, are exposed in `crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml`, and are wired through preset loading in `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs`. The remaining inline `0.2` clamp floor is still hardcoded, so a narrower amendment about that floor alone could be valid, but this amendment’s core claim that the `10.0` and `8.0` divisors are hardcoded and non-configurable is no longer true."}],"summary":"Rejected. The disputed amendment overstates the current defect: the temperature-curve divisors are already parameterized end to end, leaving only the `0.2` floor as a possible follow-up issue."}